Helix greeter
=============

The Helix login screen, run by greetd. Installing this package does not
change which login manager is active.

Switch to it (from a text console or any terminal):

    sudo systemctl disable gdm.service      # or lightdm, sddm, ...
    sudo systemctl enable --force greetd.service
    sudo reboot

Use the real unit name: on Debian and Ubuntu "gdm3" is only an alias of
gdm.service, and "systemctl disable gdm3" fails. --force replaces the
display-manager.service link that still points at the old login manager.

Switch back:

    sudo systemctl disable greetd.service
    sudo systemctl enable --force gdm.service
    sudo reboot

If the greeter does not come up, press Ctrl+Alt+F3 for a text login and
switch back as above. Its log is in `journalctl -u greetd`
(`journalctl -u greetd -b -1` for the previous boot).

Settings: copy /usr/share/doc/helix-greeter/greeter.toml.example to
/etc/helix/greeter.toml.
